# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The legacy auto-start switch must use the normal isolated app runner.
wait 15
note the work window covers it: put that away first
click-window trk_script
key w ctrl
wait 3
click-window Descriptor Demo
wait 3
expect-title Descriptor Demo
note a drag leaves footprints: MOVE paints amber, RELEASE stamps ink
press 400 300
move 430 310
move 450 315
wait 2
release 470 320
wait 6
expect-pixel 450 315 ffcb00
expect-pixel 470 320 000000
note its published menu reaches the strip over the session
write /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings GlobalMenuBar on
wait 20
click-window Descriptor Demo
wait 4
click 68 8
wait 4
expect-menu Refresh
note a second application arrives while the demo holds the first slot:
note the About asks for the PANEL role, and the host centres it --
note the same amber-rule pixel about.script pins -- rather than putting
note it one cascade step down and across from the demo.  The first slot
note cascades by zero, so only a window in a LATER slot can tell a
note honoured role from a lucky default -- the open demo menu is put
note away on the backdrop first, where the click reaches no application
click 500 620
wait 3
click 20 8
wait 4
menu-pick About this system
wait 8
expect-title About this system
expect-pixel 330 305 ffcb00
key Escape
wait 6
click-window Descriptor Demo
wait 4
click 68 8
wait 4
menu-pick Quit
wait 10
expect-no-title Descriptor Demo
quit
